globs: components/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---
- **Semantic HTML Elements:** Use semantic HTML elements for structural meaning (`<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, etc.).
- **Keyboard Navigation:** Ensure all functionality is accessible via keyboard navigation.
- **ARIA Attributes:** Implement appropriate ARIA attributes for complex UI components.
- **Color Contrast Ratios:** Maintain sufficient color contrast ratios for text and interactive elements.
- **Focus Management:** Implement visible focus indicators and manage focus for interactive elements.
- **Screen Reader Support:** Provide screen reader support with appropriate alt text and ARIA roles.
- **Responsive Design:** Ensure UI is accessible across different screen sizes and devices.
- **Image Alt Text:** Provide descriptive alt text for all images, especially in an image management application.
- **Entity Card Accessibility:** Implement accessibility features for entity cards, ensuring they're navigable and provide context.
- **Accessible Form Controls:** Use accessible form controls with proper labels and error messaging.
- **Grid View Keyboard Navigation:** Implement keyboard navigation for grid views of images and entities.
- **Visual Effects Considerations:** Ensure visual effects (animations, filters, etc.) don't cause accessibility issues.
- **Reduced Motion Support:** Respect user preferences for reduced motion with appropriate CSS media queries.
- **Off-Screen Content:** Properly manage off-screen content for screen readers with techniques like visually-hidden text.
- **Testing with Assistive Technologies:** Regularly test interfaces with screen readers and other assistive technologies.
